  "note": "Full unchanged measured-source XYZ, not independent surveys or accuracy ground truth. Native PLY input order is preserved; it is distinct from browser LOD indexing. Full-input production Delaunay TIN uses automatic edge rejection, with no extra thinning or transformed/generated coordinates. Independent archived native baseline supplies complete f64 distance bits, f64 statistics bits and scalar PLY oracle, then exits before timing. Separate archived baseline/candidate contexts share identical TIN, 4096-point original Morton chunks and fixed Rayon thread count. Each timed whole native cloud_to_mesh_par includes fresh BVH build, query ordering, parallel searches, result join and BVH destruction. No retained geometry/BVH across calls. Both builds adopt native scratch reuse, cached traversal bounds and indexed preparation. Candidate calculates the exact balanced-tree node count, initializes the existing node vector with the original capacity/growth policy, then writes disjoint preorder slices. Native meshes with at least 65536 triangles use the parallel builder; recursive nodes with at least 32768 triangles join independent child tasks on the active Rayon pool. Every centroid scan and unstable midpoint partition remains serial within its subtree. Subtree completion order cannot change node IDs, triangle offsets, partition order, bounds, retained capacities or search arithmetic. Adopted bottom-up bounds remain enabled; zero/nonfinite mesh fallback scans retain their original per-node order. Pre-sizing/initialization, scheduling and subtree work are included in whole API timing. No extra subtree node vectors, persistent cache, GPU dispatch or unsafe uninitialized nodes are introduced. Smaller meshes and builds without the native parallel feature keep the sequential builder. No WASM/browser/GPU speedup is measured. No peak process memory guarantee is made. Loading/meshing/thread-pool construction, first use, five alternating warmups, f64/summary/PLY serialization/verification and cleanup are excluded. Ten alternating timed pairs are retained without outlier removal. No builds/tests/scans/edits alongside timing. Source, executable, script, input/manifest/original PCD hashes are checked before/after. Clocks/power/scheduling/other apps/allocator/code layout/pages uncontrolled. No Python conversion, browser RPC, WASM, GPU or isolated traversal speedup claim. No GPU model identifiers collected."
